#For Documentation ---

Used Janitor package ":clean_names()" as columns that had colons 
  ("race:AfricanAmerican", "race:Asian", etc.) were replaced with a dot "." as
  colons are reserved as operators for generating sequences, thus if column names
  remained with a colon, it would result errors when running in the Data Analysis
  
Removed duplicates with dplyr: distinct() to keep unique values while avoiding
  inflated or distorted readings during Data Analysis
  
Reformatted values in smoking_history column (""former", "not current", and "ever"")
  into "Former" as these values are redundant and if kept, can generated unecessary
  labels in charts with low total values. Also reformatted "No_info" to "Unknown" to
  remove any form of ambiguity and prevent misinterpretations when ran during analysis
  
Standardized

